@startuml Component_Architecture
title MDA <-> MDH Integration - Full Component Architecture (final integrated model)
skinparam componentStyle uml2

package "MDA (existing project, read-only here)" {
  [UML Activity Diagram\n(poisson_dsc.uml)] as UML
  [ATL Transform\n(poisson_uml2cuda.atl)] as ATL
  [MDA Naive Kernel\n(mda_kernel.cu)] as MDA_KERNEL
}

package "Bridge (new work)" {
  [UML-to-MDH Bridge\n(uml_to_mdh_bridge.py)] as BRIDGE
}

package "MDH (framework + two specs)" {
  [MDH Hand-written Spec\n(poisson_handwritten.cpp)] as SPEC_HW
  [Bridge-derived Spec\n(poisson_from_uml.cpp)] as SPEC_BRIDGE
  [MDH Generator\n(cuda_generator.hpp)] as GENERATOR
}

package "Generated GPU Kernels" {
  [MDH-alone Kernel\n(poisson_1.cu, from SPEC_HW)] as K_MDH
  [Integrated Kernel\n(poisson_1.cu, from SPEC_BRIDGE)] as K_INTEGRATED
}

package "Benchmark (new work)" {
  [Serial CPU Baseline] as SERIAL
  [3-way Benchmark Harness\n(test_poisson_mda / _handwritten / _converge)] as HARNESS
}

[README.md "Results" section] as RESULTS

() "UML node pattern" as NodePattern
() "MDH spec interface" as SpecIface

UML -- NodePattern
BRIDGE ..> NodePattern : reads / requires
ATL ..> UML : reads\n(reference only,\nnot executed here)
note right of ATL
  Kept only so the bridge's
  recognized vocabulary can be
  checked against what MDA's
  own transform already hardcodes.
end note

BRIDGE --> SPEC_BRIDGE : emits

SPEC_HW -- SpecIface
SPEC_BRIDGE -- SpecIface
SpecIface )- GENERATOR : built & run by

GENERATOR --> K_MDH : generates
GENERATOR --> K_INTEGRATED : generates

note bottom of K_INTEGRATED
  Byte-for-byte identical source
  to K_MDH (verified with diff) -
  same kernel, two different specs.
end note

MDA_KERNEL --> HARNESS : benchmarked in
K_MDH --> HARNESS : benchmarked in
K_INTEGRATED --> HARNESS : benchmarked in
SERIAL --> HARNESS : baseline for

HARNESS --> RESULTS : reports 3-way speedup table

@enduml

@startuml Pipeline_Activity
title UML -> MDH Bridge - Activity Diagram (the bridge's own logic)

start
:Author UML activity diagram in Papyrus\n(SelectNode, CheckBounds, BoundsDecision,\nReadNeighbours, ApplyStencil, StoreValue);
:Bridge parses poisson_dsc.uml\nand looks for the recognized node pattern;

if (all required nodes present\nwith the expected xmi:type?) then (yes)
  :Map SelectNode -> L(1), L(2);
  :Map ReadNeighbours (top/bot/left/right)\n-> 5-point stencil neighborhood;
  :Map ApplyStencil formula -> scalar_function f;
  :Map StoreValue, no reduce loop -> result_buffer, md_hom<2,0>;
  :Emit generated/poisson_from_uml.cpp;
  :cmake && make -> build/poisson_from_uml;
  :Run executable -> poisson_1.cu, poisson_2.cu;
  :Compile benchmarks (nvcc) with matching tile -D flags;
  :Run Serial Jacobi (CPU) to convergence;
  :Run MDH-tuned kernel (GPU) to convergence;
  :Run MDA naive kernel (GPU) to convergence,\nsame serial baseline, same harness;
  :Compare iteration counts, residuals,\nmax diff, and kernel times;
  :Record 3-way speedup table in README.md;
else (no)
  :Abort with a clear error --\nthe bridge refuses to guess silently;
  end
endif
stop

@enduml

@startuml Pipeline_Sequence
title MDA <-> MDH Integration - Full Pipeline Sequence (one end-to-end run)

actor Researcher
participant "UML Model\n(poisson_dsc.uml)" as UML
participant "Bridge\n(uml_to_mdh_bridge.py)" as Bridge
participant "MDH Generator\n(cuda_generator.hpp)" as Generator
participant "Benchmark Binary\n(nvcc-built)" as Benchmark
participant "Serial CPU\nBaseline" as Serial
participant "GPU" as GPU

Researcher -> Bridge : run uml_to_mdh_bridge.py
activate Bridge
Bridge -> UML : parse poisson_dsc.uml
activate UML
UML --> Bridge : node list\n(SelectNode, ReadNeighbours, ...)
deactivate UML
Bridge -> Bridge : verify recognized pattern\n(abort if mismatched)
Bridge -> Bridge : emit poisson_from_uml.cpp
deactivate Bridge

Researcher -> Generator : cmake && make &&\nrun poisson_from_uml
activate Generator
Generator -> Generator : build md_hom spec,\nemit tiled kernel text
Generator --> Researcher : poisson_1.cu, poisson_2.cu
deactivate Generator

Researcher -> Benchmark : nvcc compile\n(test harness + kernel)
activate Benchmark
Benchmark -> Serial : run serial Jacobi\nto convergence
activate Serial
Serial --> Benchmark : iterations, time, residual
deactivate Serial

Benchmark -> GPU : launch kernel,\niterate to convergence
activate GPU
GPU --> Benchmark : iterations, time, residual
deactivate GPU

Benchmark -> Benchmark : speedup = serial time /\nGPU kernel time
Benchmark --> Researcher : print comparison table
deactivate Benchmark

note over Researcher, GPU
  Repeated for all three kernels (MDA alone,
  MDH alone, Integrated) and all three grid
  sizes (64, 128, 256) to produce the full
  results table in README.md.
end note

@enduml
